# PART 2 – OWN HOST & DISCOVERED HOSTS

## 2.1 INTRODUCTION

This section describes the identification of the attacker machine and the discovery of active hosts within the assigned laboratory network. 
Nmap was used to perform host discovery to identify devices that were active and responding within the network range.

The purpose of this activity was to identify the available hosts before proceeding with network service detection.

2.2 ATTACKER HOST 

The attacker machine used in this activity was Kali Linux. 
The network configuration was examined using Linux networking commands to identify the machine's hostname, network interface and assigned IP address.



| Configuration | Result |
|---|---|
